# chrome tiers (TUI-DESIGN-2 §4.1): boxed at 24x80 (the console's top edge carries the badge), flat at 12x60 (the badge
# leads the status left zone, no box rows), boxed again at 24x80; the shrink segment may cost one clear, the grow none.
# Every expect precedes the sleep that follows its resize: the driver's `sleep` drains (and consumes) the pty, so a row
# that arrived during a sleep can never be matched afterwards.
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect ╭─ (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*jev-only
expect sess \$
sleep 0.3
resize 12 60
expect jev-only(?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* · idle
sleep 0.5
mark shrunk
resize 24 80
expect ╭─ (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*jev-only
sleep 0.5
mark grown
send Z
expect (?:›|>) Z
send \x03
expect Say hi
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
